{"actions":[{"date":"2026-09-08","source":"House floor actions","text":"Placed on the Union Calendar, Calendar No. 702.","type":"Calendars"},{"date":"2026-09-08","source":"House floor actions","text":"Reported (Amended) by the Committee on Education and Workforce. H. Rept. 119-802.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2026-09-08","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Reported (Amended) by the Committee on Education and Workforce. H. Rept. 119-802.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2026-07-21","source":"House committee actions","text":"Ordered to be Reported (Amended) by the Yeas and Nays: 18 - 15.","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2026-07-21","source":"House committee actions","text":"Committee Consideration and Mark-up Session Held","type":"Committee"},{"date":"2025-09-10","source":"House floor actions","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Education and Workforce.","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-09-10","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"},{"date":"2025-09-10","source":"Library of Congress","text":"Introduced in House","type":"IntroReferral"}],"amendments":{"items":[],"total":0},"analysis_status":"scored","bipartisan_band":null,"chamber":"House","committees":[{"activities":[{"date":"2026-09-08","name":"Reported By"},{"date":"2026-07-21","name":"Markup By"},{"date":"2025-09-10","name":"Referred To"}],"chamber":"House","code":"hsed00","name":"Education and Workforce Committee","subcommittees":[]}],"cosponsor_count":158,"fetched_at":"2026-10-25T21:25:38+00:00","history":[{"day":"2026-10-25","importance":50,"viability":64.8}],"id":"119-hr-5267","importance":50,"importance_band":"moderate","importance_detail":{"consistent":true,"dimension_mean":51.0,"dimensions":[{"assessment":"Potentially affects millions of franchise establishments and workers across the United States economy.","evidence":"franchises employed approximately 5 percent of all workers in the United States, which was approximately 8,400,000 workers.","evidence_verified":true,"key":"population","score":75},{"assessment":"Establishes a uniform legal definition of joint employment that limits franchisor liability unless specific direct control over employment terms is exercised.","evidence":"a franchisor may be considered a joint employer of the employees of a franchisee only if the franchisor possesses and exercises substantial direct and immediate control","evidence_verified":true,"key":"magnitude","score":50},{"assessment":"Does not involve federal spending or revenue changes, focusing entirely on labor law standards and legal liability definitions.","evidence":null,"evidence_verified":false,"key":"fiscal","score":15},{"assessment":"Amends both the National Labor Relations Act and the Fair Labor Standards Act of 1938 to introduce standardized franchise employment criteria.","evidence":"The National Labor Relations Act (29 U.S.C. 151 et seq.) is amended by adding at the end the following","evidence_verified":true,"key":"scope","score":55},{"assessment":"Provides a permanent legal standard for franchise relationships, though it exempts pending proceedings commenced before enactment.","evidence":"This Act, and the amendments made by this Act, shall not apply to any proceeding that is commenced before the date of enactment of this Act.","evidence_verified":true,"key":"duration","score":60}],"missing_information":["The exact number of pending legal proceedings or specific economic cost savings for franchisors are not quantified."],"rationale":"The American Franchise Act clarifies joint-employer standards under the National Labor Relations Act and the Fair Labor Standards Act specifically for the franchise business model, requiring substantial direct and immediate control for a franchisor to be considered a joint employer.","score":50},"importance_meta":{"generated_at":"2026-10-25T21:26:35+00:00","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","source_basis":"text","source_urls":["https://www.congress.gov/119/bills/hr5267/BILLS-119hr5267rh.htm"